# Pygame Avocado Shooter: Core Architecture

## Project layout (current)

- `main.py` — game loop, input, draw helpers, sprite load/blit
- `game/settings.py` — window size, speeds, colors, sprite path/size
- `game/camera.py` — `Camera` dataclass, `world_to_screen`, `screen_to_world`
- `img/` — hero/enemy art (hero: `bravocado-points-one-hand-no-bg.PNG`, transparent PNG)
- `docs/plans/bravocado.plan.md` — step-by-step roadmap

## World vs screen (implemented)

- Use **world coordinates** (`pygame.math.Vector2`) for simulation: today `player_pos`; later `player.pos`, `enemy.pos`, `bullet.pos`.
- Player is **drawn at screen center** `(WINDOW_W/2, WINDOW_H/2)`; world scrolls via camera.
- Camera follows player: `camera.pos = player_pos` (sync each frame after movement).
- Transforms live in `game/camera.py`:
  - `world_to_screen(p) = p - camera.pos + (WINDOW_W/2, WINDOW_H/2)`
  - `screen_to_world(s) = s + camera.pos - (WINDOW_W/2, WINDOW_H/2)`
- World-space grid uses `world_to_screen`; player sprite does **not** (always centered).

## Motion & timing

- **dt-based motion** (seconds): `pos += vel * dt`; `dt = clock.tick(FPS_CAP) / 1000.0`.
- Speeds in `game/settings.py` are **pixels per second** (e.g. `PLAYER_SPEED = 320`).
- Use `pygame.time.get_ticks()` for cadence timers (auto-fire 500ms, contact damage cooldown) — not implemented yet.

## Planned (not in codebase yet)

- Lightweight entities in `game/entities.py` (dataclass or simple class).
- Bullets, enemies, circle collisions, HP, `PLAYING` / `WIN` / `GAME_OVER` + full restart.

When adding features, extend existing modules before growing `main.py`; keep constants in `game/settings.py`.
